  "decision_needed": [
    {
      "question": "Rural fire reimbursement 22,483 is printed under Other Financing Sources in the governmental funds statement (p6) but as a general revenue in the Statement of Activities (p3) and an operating receipt in the budget schedule (p9). Should it count as a receipt?",
      "amount": 22483,
      "recorded_as": "other_financing (as printed in the governmental funds statement)",
      "source_page": 6
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit (basis recorded as cash). Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures, and Changes in Fund Balances (Total Governmental Funds, pp5-6; funds General, Road, Debt Service; the p4 balance sheet calls the Road Fund 'Street Fund'). Sale of bonds 1,580,000 is printed among revenues, so it is a receipt (Bond Proceeds). Fund balance roll-forward: 2,489,284 + 2,144,869 - 3,790,954 + 22,483 + 1,622,330 - 1,653,654 = 834,358. Cash from the governmental funds statement (p4): cash 712,250 + county treasurer 4,592 (2022: 2,337,256 + 6,508); certificates of deposit as investments. Business-type (Water, Sewer) lines from the modified cash proprietary statement (p8), which ties to the Statement of Activities (expenses 272,520, charges 196,107, grants 342,971, investment income 48, transfers 31,324); net position 3,612,989 restated by (981,000) to 2,631,989, ending 2,929,919. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (includes capital assets and debt, so not the funds statement). Detail = per-fund columns of the governmental funds and proprietary funds statements; the only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budgetary comparison (pp9-10), not used to avoid double counting. Read pages 1-10 of 10"
}
